# CMPG313 Lab 1 – YOLOv8 Object Detection

## Overview
As part of my coursework, I trained a YOLOv8 model to detect an object or action involving myself, using data I collected and labeled. This project allowed me to explore machine learning workflows, from dataset creation to model evaluation, and gain hands-on experience with Teachable Machine. Through this process, I not only strengthened my practical skills in computer vision and object detection but also considered real-world applications for AI in personal and professional contexts.

## Tools Used
- Python 3.14.0
- YOLOv8 (Ultralytics)
- OpenCV
- GitHub

## Features
- Object detection on images
- Object detection and tracking on video
- Real-time detection using webcam

## How to Run
1. Install required libraries:
pip install ultralytics opencv-python

2. Run the script:
python lab_1.py

## Example Outputs
The repository includes screenshots and output videos showing:
- Detection on an image
- Detection on traffic video
- Detection using webcam

